<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 73 0 R
/T (Rather than replacing traditional programming, low-code complements it by accelerating the development of internal tools, automation solutions, and business applications. Many organizations now adopt a hybrid approach, using traditional development for mission-critical systems while leveraging low-code platforms like UiPath for rapid automation and workflow management. Choosing the right approach ultimately depends on project complexity, timeline, budget, and long-term business objectives.)
/E (Rather than replacing traditional programming, low-code complements it by accelerating the development of internal tools, automation solutions, and business applications. Many organizations now adopt a hybrid approach, using traditional development for mission-critical systems while leveraging low-code platforms like UiPath for rapid automation and workflow management. Choosing the right approach ultimately depends on project complexity, timeline, budget, and long-term business objectives.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
